Discovered during forced P6.M1 host validation on exact source3626221f: test_c2c_relay_managed child in B298 cap-crossing case raises Unix_error(EINTR,waitpid) at ocaml/cli/c2c_relay_managed.ml403. Parent suite still exits0, yielding nested failure and duplicate suite/test counts. Required: interrupt-safe child waits in relay supervisor; deterministic signal regression; forked supervisor test failures must terminate child without re-entering Alcotest and be asserted by parent. Preserve signal shutdown/restart semantics and PID-generation ownership. Critical validation blocker for T3 host slice. Reproduce/log from x-p35 /tmp/t3-c2c-validation-deps/c2c-final-realroot-runtest.log (confirm actual final filename from validation_env). Keep fix narrow, separate worktree, focused tests on x-p35 and independent review.

Decision: retry only EINTR at every waitpid in the relay supervisor; preserve ECHILD and other errors. After a restart reap, a concurrently received Stop returns cleanly rather than launching a replacement. Tests use a deterministic syscall seam for interrupted/non-interrupted status and error behavior, plus a real forked supervisor held in termination until Stop arrives. A fixture child wrapper catches exceptions and calls Unix._exit, preventing inherited Alcotest reentry; B298 parents now check clean supervisor exit. Changes isolated to two relay files in .worktrees/b367-relay-eintr; test runtime remains x-p35 only. Independent Terra review running through a currently authenticated configured Codex instance (default instance became unauthenticated).